The robot sim-robot-002 is in the "Idle" phase and its emergency stop (estop) is stopped (status.estopState=Stopped). This means that sim-robot-002 is currently not taking any work because it is idle and its estop has been triggered. To resume its operations, an emergency stop must be cleared. You can request a zone stop to clear the estop state, but note that this is not an emergency path and requires approval from a named person. 

If you wish to proceed with clearing the estop, you can request a zone stop as follows:

```json
{
  "name": "request_zone_stop",
  "arguments": {
    "zoneName": "warehouse-a",
    "reason": "Clearing emergency stop for sim-robot-002",
    "namespace": "warehouse-a"
  }
}
```

However, I cannot clear an emergency stop or resume a robot. This action must be approved by a named person.
